module bankr-tnm-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }
import frbp.events.{ FirstMeetingDate, InvoluntarySummonsServed, OrderForReliefEntered }

// The Bankr. M.D. Tenn. court's own periods, counted under FRBP 9006(a),
// the FRCP 6(a) method: the Local Rules of Court amended and restated as of
// July 28, 2025. The FRBP periods (schedules, claims, the chapter 13 plan,
// discharge, dischargeability, exemptions, the adversary answer, appeals)
// are lit/frbp's and are not declared again. HOLE: the general motion
// notice and objection periods live in the separate LBR 9013-1 Motion
// Practice Procedures (LBR 9013-1, 4001-1(g)), which are not vendored
// (sources/bankr-tnm/PROVENANCE.md), so no period of that document is
// declared; the administrative orders listed at /substantive-
// administrative-orders were not read for rule amendments, so whether any
// later order amends these rules is unconfirmed. Stated in the rules but
// not declared: the business-day and clock-time periods (first-day matters
// heard within two business days and 24 hours' notice of a first-day
// hearing, 2081-1, 2081-2(i); a complex case notice two business days
// before the petition and hearing agendas and replies two business days
// before an omnibus hearing, 2081-2; 24 hours' notice to the United States
// Trustee before a motion to withdraw, 2091-1; a joint continuance by the
// second business day before a stay hearing, 4001-1(d); the chapter 13 stay
// extension motion within five business days of the petition, its objection
// deadline four business days before the hearing and its certificate of
// service within three business days, 4001-1(h); the rent deposit by the
// next business day, 4002-1(c); briefs by noon on the second business day
// before the hearing, 9013-2(a); certificates of service within three
// business days, 9013-3(a); the fourth-business-day limbs of the contested
// matter disclosures, 9014-1); calendar-day deadlines (monthly operating
// reports by the 21st of the following month and quarterly post-
// confirmation reports by the 21st of the month after the quarter, 2015-2);
// recurring periods (the master service list every 7 days for the first 30
// days and every 30 after, 2081-2; interim compensation every 120 days,
// 2081-2(m)); hearing settings (a matter filed at least 21 days before an
// omnibus hearing is heard at it, 2081-2(j); the extend-stay hearing within
// 30 days of the petition and its objection deadline at least 14 days after
// service, 4001-1(h)); the clerk's own acts (a denied sealed document held
// 14 days, 9018-1(c)); the rules' own effective date 60 days after notice
// (9029-1(a)); the 45 days of § 521(a)(1) that a Certificate of Compliance
// recites (1017-2, 11 U.S.C. § 521(i)); 60 days of insurance coverage from
// the meeting and delivery of notice three days after mailing (4070-1); and
// the deadlines that are another date (proof of insurance at or before the
// meeting, 4070-1(a)).

/// A notice or order converting a case to chapter 7 from another chapter is
/// filed (LBR 1017-1).
event ConversionNoticed()
/// A List of Creditors that does not conform to the Mailing List
/// Guidelines, or an amendment adding creditors after the petition, is
/// filed (LBR 2002-1(a)).
event CreditorListFiled()
/// The trustee's or United States trustee's Report of Nonappearance, Notice
/// and Motion to Dismiss is entered (LBR 2003-1(a)).
event NonappearanceDismissalEntered()
/// The debtor obtains a rescheduled meeting of creditors date (LBR
/// 2003-1(b)).
event RescheduledMeetingObtained()
/// A meeting of creditors is scheduled to be held (LBR 2003-1(c)).
event MeetingOfCreditorsScheduled()
/// A professional's Monthly Statement of fees and expenses in a complex
/// chapter 11 case is served (LBR 2081-2(m)).
event MonthlyStatementServed()
/// An omnibus hearing date in a complex chapter 11 case is set (LBR
/// 2081-2(j)).
event OmnibusHearingScheduled()
/// The trustee gives a secured creditor written notice that it failed to
/// provide the information LBR 3001-1(a) requires (LBR 3001-1(b)).
event NoncomplianceNoticeSent()
/// An agreed order granting stay relief or abandonment without a motion is
/// entered (LBR 4001-1(f)).
event AgreedStayOrderEntered()
/// A creditor takes possession of a motor vehicle on a lapse of insurance
/// (LBR 4070-1(c)(4)).
event VehicleRepossessed()
/// A no asset notice issues and is not superseded by an asset notice (LBR
/// 6007-1(a)).
event NoAssetNoticeIssued()
/// The non-moving party files its response to a summary judgment motion,
/// asserting additional facts (LBR 7056-1(c)).
event SummaryJudgmentResponseFiled()
/// The paper commencing a contested matter is served (LBR 9014-1(c)).
event ContestedMatterServed()
/// A hearing of a contested matter is scheduled to be held (LBR 9014-1(c)).
event ContestedHearingScheduled()
/// An objection or response in a contested matter is served (LBR
/// 9014-1(d)).
event ContestedResponseServed()
/// A matter or proceeding is finally determined (LBR 9070-1).
event FinalDetermination()

/// LBR 1017-1: within 14 days after a notice or order converting a case to
/// chapter 7, the debtor files new lists, statements and schedules
/// (Schedule C at the debtor's discretion) with a notice of added
/// creditors.
deadline conversion-schedules-period: 14.days after ConversionNoticed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 1017-1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 2002-1(a): if the List of Creditors does not conform to the
/// guidelines or is amended to add creditors, the debtor mails the meeting
/// of creditors notice to the entities affected within 7 days of filing the
/// list or amendment.
deadline added-creditor-notice-period: 7.days after CreditorListFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 2002-1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 2003-1(a): an objection to dismissal for the debtor's nonappearance
/// at the meeting of creditors is filed within 21 days from entry of the
/// Notice and Motion to Dismiss; otherwise the clerk enters an Order of
/// Dismissal.
deadline nonappearance-objection-period: 21.days after NonappearanceDismissalEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 2003-1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 2003-1(b): the debtor gives notice of a rescheduled meeting of
/// creditors to the trustees, creditors and parties in interest no later
/// than 7 days after obtaining the date.
deadline rescheduled-meeting-notice-period: 7.days after RescheduledMeetingObtained() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 2003-1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 2003-1(c): motions and orders to produce prisoners for a meeting of
/// creditors are filed at least 14 days before the scheduled meeting.
deadline prisoner-production-period: 14.days before MeetingOfCreditorsScheduled() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 2003-1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 2081-2: an involuntary debtor eligible for complex case treatment
/// files its notice of election with its answer or within 21 days after
/// service of the summons, whichever is earlier.
deadline complex-election-period: 21.days after InvoluntarySummonsServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 2081-2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 2081-2(j): objections to a matter set for an omnibus hearing are
/// filed at least 7 days before the omnibus hearing date.
deadline omnibus-objection-period: 7.days before OmnibusHearingScheduled() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 2081-2(j)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 2081-2(m): objections to a professional's Monthly Statement are
/// filed within 14 days of its service; after that the debtor may pay 80%
/// of the undisputed fees and expenses.
deadline monthly-statement-objection-period: 14.days after MonthlyStatementServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 2081-2(m)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 3001-1(b): a creditor that fails to cure its noncompliance within 21
/// days after the trustee's written notice is exposed to preclusion and
/// other relief.
deadline lien-information-cure-period: 21.days after NoncomplianceNoticeSent() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 3001-1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 3015-1(d): a written objection to confirmation of a chapter 13 plan
/// is filed at least 5 calendar days before the meeting of creditors (an
/// oral objection may be raised at the meeting).
deadline chapter13-confirmation-objection-period: 5.days before FirstMeetingDate() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 3015-1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 4001-1(f)(1): an agreed order granting stay relief or abandonment
/// without a motion orders that any objection be filed within 14 days of
/// its entry.
deadline agreed-stay-order-objection-period: 14.days after AgreedStayOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 4001-1(f)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 4002-1(a)(5): in an involuntary case, the natural person who will
/// perform the debtor's acts is identified no later than 14 days after
/// entry of the order for relief.
deadline involuntary-responsible-person-period: 14.days after OrderForReliefEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 4002-1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 4070-1(c)(4): within 7 days after taking possession of a motor
/// vehicle for lapse of insurance, the creditor moves for relief from the §
/// 362 stay.
deadline vehicle-stay-motion-period: 7.days after VehicleRepossessed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 4070-1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 6007-1(a): in a no asset case, abandonment is effective 14 days
/// after the notice unless an objection is filed.
deadline no-asset-abandonment-period: 14.days after NoAssetNoticeIssued() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 6007-1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 7056-1(c): the moving party's reply statement to additional facts is
/// filed within 14 days of the filing of the non-moving party's response.
deadline summary-judgment-reply-period: 14.days after SummaryJudgmentResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 7056-1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 9014-1(c): in a contested matter outside the Motion Practice
/// Procedures' 'if objection' process, a response or objection is filed and
/// served by the earlier of 21 days after service of the commencing paper
/// and 7 days before a scheduled hearing.
deadline contested-response-service-period: 21.days after ContestedMatterServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 9014-1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 9014-1(c): the hearing limb of that earlier-of deadline, 7 days
/// before any scheduled hearing of the contested matter.
deadline contested-response-hearing-period: 7.days before ContestedHearingScheduled() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 9014-1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 9014-1(d)(2)(D): when the movant elects pretrial disclosures, the
/// initial disclosures of witnesses and documents (paragraphs (A) and (B))
/// are completed no later than 7 calendar days after service of the
/// objection or response (or by the fourth business day before the hearing,
/// if earlier).
deadline initial-disclosure-period: 7.days after ContestedResponseServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 9014-1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 9014-1(d)(2)(D): the expert witness disclosures of paragraph (C) are
/// completed no later than 14 days after service of the response (or by the
/// fourth business day before the hearing, if earlier).
deadline expert-disclosure-period: 14.days after ContestedResponseServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 9014-1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LBR 9070-1: after final determination of a matter or proceeding, parties
/// have 28 days to withdraw exhibits.
deadline exhibit-withdrawal-period: 28.days after FinalDetermination() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. Tenn. LBR 9070-1"
{
  forum frcp
}
